From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:18:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a provider's passFields carry a request's unknown
 fields on a cross-protocol build (#7376)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A client that talks the Anthropic entry to an OpenAI-compatible
upstream loses top-level fields the translation doesn't know, such as
chat_template_kwargs, and some vendors' reasoning toggles ride on
exactly such a field: the request went out without it and nothing said
so (imxzt, #7376 — their diagnosis took hours).

provider.PassFields (off by default) names the body keys a provider
wants carried. The entry parsers keep the body as it came beside the
keys their schema consumes (rawBody/knownTop); buildFor picks the
allowlisted unknown ones per provider; every translated build (Chat,
Responses, Gemini, Vertex, Anthropic) merges them where its own schema
leaves a key free — a key the build set is the build's, and a request
relayed as it came forwards everything verbatim as it always has. The
providers editor gets the field beside Request headers to pass.

Run (darwin/arm64, upstream/main 604f707d2 + this commit):
- TestPassFieldsCarryUnknownTopFields / …OffDrops / …NeverOverwrite /
  …CarryFromChatEntryToAnthropicUpstream: red at the drop before this
  commit's gateway half, green after
- ablation: the buildFor wiring out → the same two reds; restored →
  green

